+++ b/fx/prod28_runtime_provenance.py
@@ -0,0 +1,244 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""PROD-28 re-take: is the code/bundle/model the live producer stack is RUNNING the code on disk?
+
+AUDIT_PROD's PROD-28 verified this against com.hsy.shadowloop PID 10900 / sidecar 30943 /
+combolive 30944.  The Mac rebooted 2026-09-14 15:43:56Z (kern.boottime) and all three daemons
+restarted at 15:45:14Z, so those PIDs no longer exist and that verification is stale.  This device
+re-takes it against the processes that are actually running, without substituting `git HEAD` for
+evidence and without touching the daemons.
+
+macOS has no /proc, so "which bytes is this process executing" is established by an interval
+argument rather than by reading the process's memory:
+
+    if a source file's mtime is EARLIER than the process's start time, the file has not changed
+    since the process loaded it, so the bytes on disk now are the bytes it loaded.
+
+That is the whole claim, and it is falsifiable: any file with mtime >= process start is reported as
+RUNNING_CODE_UNKNOWN, because the process may be executing content that no longer exists on disk
+(the "patch on disk is not the patch running" family).  `lsof -p` is recorded as corroboration for
+the files the process still holds open (a long-lived Python has usually closed its .py sources, so
+absence from lsof is not evidence of anything and is not treated as such).
+
+Two different lifetimes are handled separately:
+  - shadow_loop_v3.py runs inside the long-lived producer process -> compare against ITS start.
+  - combo_stage.py and sidecar_blend.py are launched fresh by their daemons every anchor, so the
